<title>USA: Boston Communications CEO resigns.</title>
<headline>Boston Communications CEO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>WOBURN, Mass. 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boston Communications Group Inc said Friday that George Hertz had resigned as president, chief executive and a director for personal reasons.</p>
<p>Hertz, who joined the company in March 1996, directed Boston Communications in its transition to a public company last year.</p>
<p>Boston Communications said Paul Tobin, currently its chairman, had been named acting president and chief executive. It said its board was seeking a new chief executive.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
